  data: {
    LLM: "Try to hold two strong suits that total to seven (such as 2s and 5s). This gives you flexibility with the matador matching rule.\n\nThe 0-0 (blank-blank) is the most valuable tile - it guarantees a play and can block one end of the train. Save matadors to change the end of the train when you don't have a matching tile.\n\nIf you have a double, try to set up an arm in phase one that will let you play it in phase two. For example, with the 6-6 double as spinner and you hold 5-6 and 5-5, play 5-6 on the spinner to guarantee playing 5-5 on the next turn.",
    Player: "Try to hold two strong suits that total to seven (such as 2s and 5s). This gives you flexibility with the matador matching rule.\n\nThe 0-0 (blank-blank) is the most valuable tile - it guarantees a play and can block one end of the train. Save matadors to change the end of the train when you don't have a matching tile.\n\nIf you have a double, try to set up an arm in phase one that will let you play it in phase two. For example, with the 6-6 double as spinner and you hold 5-6 and 5-5, play 5-6 on the spinner to guarantee playing 5-5 on the next turn.",
